From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: add the erhai SC8547A charge pump and PPS engine

The SC8547A charge pump driver, the erhai PPS engine and the SC8547A
binding as of erhai-v0.7.2, with their Kconfig and Makefile entries (the
CPS8601 pen charger from the same erhai commits is left out: the pen is
not in scope here). The battery manager side (erhai_pps_register(),
serialisation with fixed PD and suspend) is already in 2101.

erhai_pps engages only for PD_PPS adapters and falls back to the ordinary
5 V contract on any failure; it charges fast only between 12 and 44 C and
below its SoC stop limit, and exits to 5 V before system suspend. The
module parameter erhai_pps.pps_enable switches it at run time.

Both files carry the GPL-2.0-only notice of the OnePlus vendor sources
they were ported from (see their headers).

erhai commits, oldest first (authors as recorded there):
  5cd5e6df7 yzddmr6: dt-bindings: power: supply: describe Southchip SC8547A charge pumps
  1264c7f48 yzddmr6: power: supply: add protected SC8547A charge pump control
  7d7c1f6f0 yzddmr6: power: supply: sc8547a: leave initial voltage entry policy to the controller
  af5949fb9 yading <woshiyading@163.com>: power: supply: import the Erhai PPS and wireless pen charging drivers
  440c72cd1 yzddmr6: power: supply: serialize Erhai PPS with the battery manager and suspend
  14516496a yzddmr6: power: supply: complete PPS handover and pen charger teardown
  b46305b07 yzddmr6: power: supply: erhai_pps: charge fast only between 12 and 44 °C

[opd2413: files taken whole from erhai-v0.7.2; Kconfig/Makefile entries
 without CPS8601. The board DTS already carries both SC8547A nodes.]
